-- title:
--   Krull dimension at most one away from q
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ not divisible by $q$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite. Assume two variable-change stability hypotheses over all $A_0$-algebras $T$: that for every Weierstrass curve $W/T$ and variable change $C$ a level-$\ell$ datum $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ satisfying the level-$\ell$ conditions (both points satisfy the affine equation of $W$, $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$, and both independence elements $\prod_{1\le a\le(\ell-1)/2}(x\,\Psi_a^2(x')-\Phi_a(x'))$ are units) transforms to such a datum for $C\bullet W$; and that the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt` for a cyclic $p^k$-kernel polynomial (degree at most $\varphi(p^k)/2$ and monic in that degree, $h\cdot\operatorname{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}} \mid \operatorname{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and the divisibility of the relevant `smulNumerator`s; the two-kernel conditions when $p^k=2$) is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`. Let $\mathcal G$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord-and-tangent (realised on points over fields) and with identity section cut out in the origin chart by $x/y = z/y = 0$; let $\mathcal T$ be a transport of raw Drinfeld pairs (a curve together with two sections) preserving Drinfeld $q$-bases, assumed to be a section transport, i.e. compatible with the `Proj` morphisms coming from variable changes and from coefficient maps. Assume moreover that such graded ring homomorphisms realising variable changes and coefficient changes exist, compatibly with the irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be an absolute level-moduli package for the datum `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q` — a product of the $\Gamma_0$ prime-power kernel component for $M'$, the level-$\ell$ component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component, rigidified and passed to its moduli datum — so $P_0$ consists of an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point representing the functor, and assume $B_0$ is of finite type over $A_0$. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B_0$ with the image of $q$ not in $\mathfrak m$, the Krull dimension of the localisation $(B_0)_{\mathfrak m}$ is at most $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that the fine full-level moduli ring $B_0$ has relative dimension at most one over the base at closed points of the generic fibre: away from the residue characteristic $q$ the local rings are at most one-dimensional. It is obtained from the integrality of $B_0$ over the subalgebra generated by the $j$-invariant together with the fact that an integral ring extension does not raise Krull dimension, and it feeds the normality and domain properties of the $q$-adic completion used in the study of the local behaviour of the modular curve at $q$.
